<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- FacetUI: stop being translucent when there is no blur to show through.

         Battery saver and the developer option "disable blurs" both switch
         cross-window blur off, and some GPUs never had it. In that state a
         panel at 77% over unblurred, scrolling content is HARDER to read than
         an opaque one - the design has quietly become worse than no design.

         With this on, a surface that asked for background blur and did not get
         it composites over an opaque layer of its own colour instead. Tint and
         corners are kept; only the transparency goes.

         It also solidifies when high contrast text is enabled, which is the
         nearest thing Android has to a reduce-transparency setting - and means
         the existing "disable blurs" toggle doubles as one.

         Stock is false. Needs patches/framework/0002. -->
    <bool name="facetui_solidify_when_no_blur">true</bool>
</resources>
